browser XHR FOLLOWS the guest fall-through's 302 to "/" (home); that redirected GET is itself a session request and consumes the key.
fixed tree 29606d8c3, own server :8155, clone qa4155. Held owner session, XHR 403 first, then:

jar g: ajax POST switch-to-commission -> 403 JSON auth-003
  poll1 (XHR, redirect FOLLOWED, like a browser) final=http://localhost:8155/ code=200 hops=1
  poll2 (XHR, redirect FOLLOWED)                 final=http://localhost:8155/ code=200 hops=1
  reload (plain navigation)                      -> 302 loc=[http://localhost:8155/]        <-- key already gone: no login, no copy (= base behaviour)
jar h: ajax POST switch-to-commission -> 403 JSON auth-003
  poll1 (XHR, redirect NOT followed)             code=302 loc=[http://localhost:8155/]
  poll2 (XHR, redirect NOT followed)             code=302 loc=[http://localhost:8155/]
  reload (plain navigation)                      -> 302 loc=[http://localhost:8155/login/vendor]   <-- survives only when the redirect is not followed (what a no-redirect test client measures)

Real browser (Chrome), same shape: after the 403 on item/variant-combination, two $.get('/vendor-panel/get-store-data', dataType json):
  network: GET get-store-data [302] -> GET / [200]  (twice), then reload GET item/add-new [302] -> GET / [200]  (no login page, no copy)
